<%# Percentage hero result (DESIGN.md §4 "Hero-result"): a surface card with a 5px coral
    left rule and a big tabular-nums number — the page's headline answer. The selected
    mode returns a single result key (value | percent | base, ARCHITECTURE.md §4); that
    key drives the caption and whether the number reads as a percentage (the % suffix).
    `calc:` is a valid Calculators::Percentage (the empty + error states are handled one
    level up in _result.html.erb). %>
<% key, value = calc.result.first %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent"><%= percentage_result_caption(calc.mode) %></p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink">
        <%= percentage_display(value) %><%= "%" if key == :percent %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted"><%= percentage_result_detail(calc) %></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
